# Consulate pages that moved. Netlify and Cloudflare Workers static assets both
# read this file. Every rule without a placeholder or splat must come before
# the first rule with one: Cloudflare counts every rule after that first one as
# one with a placeholder, keeps only 100 of those (and 2,000 without) and skips
# the rest without failing the deploy. In this order the two hosts also agree
# on which rule applies: Netlify follows the first rule that matches, and
# Cloudflare the rules without a placeholder before the others. Cloudflare
# follows a rule even where a page exists, so no rule may match an existing
# page. scripts/check-redirects.mjs checks all of this after the build: it
# drops from out/_redirects any rule that matches a page, and fails the build
# on a rule without a placeholder or splat after one with, or past either
# limit.

